id: pm-jhpby4
title: "ADR: Ordering assurance partitions evidence-cited blocks from uncited blocks"
description: Authorize the blocks ratchet to preserve its anti-fabrication ceiling over non-evidence rows while separately flooring evidence-cited ordering.
type: Decision
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-20T20:11:18.429Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-20T20:11:42.799Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-20T20:11:42.036Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-20T20:11:42.036Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: The existing blocks ceiling is retargeted to total blocks minus evidence-cited blocks; Evidence-cited blocks receive an independent non-regression floor; Both assertions carry executable boundary negative controls and remain blocking in graph-composition
goal: Provable history
objective: Keep anti-fabrication and recovered ordering simultaneously enforceable
value: Evidence-backed historical ordering can grow without weakening graph governance
impact: Unblocks pm-c90tfh and its three ordering-lineage dependents
outcome: Provenance-partitioned blocking assertions replace one contradictory global count
why_now: The live global blocks ceiling is exactly saturated and rejected the required evidence-backed edges
parent: pm-m2u1
resolution: "Accepted ADR: preserve the uncited blocks ceiling and independently floor evidence-cited blocks."
expected_result: "Evidence-backed ordering can grow without permitting uncited directional-edge growth, and recovered evidence cannot be silently removed."
actual_result: The SDK now measures exact and prefix provenance partitions; the live declarations keep the 243 uncited ceiling and add an evidence floor with adjacent negative controls.
