close_reason: "Accepted: graph assurance partitions blocks by explicit evidence provenance, retains the uncited anti-fabrication ceiling, and independently protects recovered ordering with a floor."
body: "## Context\nThe existing blocking assertion counts all blocks rows identically. The live population was exactly at its ceiling, while accepted graph reconstruction requires adding ordering edges backed by recorded evidence.\n\n## Decision\nRetain total blocks as a diagnostic measurement. Define evidence-cited blocks by the explicit evidence: source-kind prefix. Define uncited blocks as total minus evidence-cited. Move the existing anti-fabrication ceiling to the uncited population and add a floor over evidence-cited rows. Both remain blocking and carry adjacent pass/fail negative controls.\n\n## Consequences\nAdding an evidence-cited ordering edge cannot spend anti-fabrication headroom. Deleting recovered ordering fails the evidence floor. Adding a block without the evidence prefix fails the uncited ceiling. Changing either population still requires a verified Decision."
